            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A comment that is a whole disabled form carries no reason and no attribution, unlike a TODO/FIXME marker. It is code nobody runs, drifting silently out of sync with whatever replaced it. Version control already remembers deleted code, so the comment adds nothing a `git log` would not."
              },
              "id": "commented-out-code",
              "properties": {
                "category": "dead-code",
                "fixable": false,
                "rationale": "A comment that is a whole disabled form carries no reason and no attribution, unlike a TODO/FIXME marker. It is code nobody runs, drifting silently out of sync with whatever replaced it. Version control already remembers deleted code, so the comment adds nothing a `git log` would not.",
                "severity": "warning",
                "tags": []
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a comment whose entire body is a balanced s-expression rather than prose"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A file loads by evaluating its top-level forms in order. defun/defmacro/defclass and friends only install a definition, so a forward reference inside one is ordinary — by the time it runs, the file has finished loading. defvar/defparameter and every other top-level form run immediately, and a forward reference inside one depends on the file's current order to work at all."
              },
              "id": "execution-order-dependency",
              "properties": {
                "category": "suspicious",
                "fixable": false,
                "rationale": "A file loads by evaluating its top-level forms in order. defun/defmacro/defclass and friends only install a definition, so a forward reference inside one is ordinary — by the time it runs, the file has finished loading. defvar/defparameter and every other top-level form run immediately, and a forward reference inside one depends on the file's current order to work at all.",
                "severity": "warning",
                "tags": []
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a top-level form that runs at load time and references a name this file only defines later"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A file built only from definitions and value bindings can be reordered, split, or reloaded piecemeal without changing behaviour. A file with many top-level forms that run for effect — bare calls, setf, let used for a side effect — is a sequence: each form only means what it means in the order it was written."
              },
              "id": "declarative-style-score",
              "properties": {
                "category": "suspicious",
                "fixable": false,
                "rationale": "A file built only from definitions and value bindings can be reordered, split, or reloaded piecemeal without changing behaviour. A file with many top-level forms that run for effect — bare calls, setf, let used for a side effect — is a sequence: each form only means what it means in the order it was written.",
                "severity": "warning",
                "tags": []
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a file whose fraction of purely-declarative top-level forms falls below a threshold"
              }
            }
          ]
